    <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">litmus <span class="badge badge-beta">beta</span></h2>
    <p>ML-powered malware classifier for supply-chain security. Uses
    <a href="/cleave/">cleave</a> static analysis to extract capabilities,
    then classifies threat level — built for security engineers and automated
    pipelines alike.</p>

    <h2>Capabilities</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>File scanning</strong> — scan files, directories, and archives against a local <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/litmus-models/" target="_blank">ML model</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <pre class="install-block"># macOS (Homebrew)
$ brew tap atomdrift/tap https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/homebrew-tap.git
$ brew install atomdrift/tap/litmus

# From source
$ make install</pre>

    <h2>Usage</h2>
    <pre class="install-block">$ litmus scan /path/to/file</pre>

    <p style="margin-top: 16px; padding: 10px 14px; background: #fef9c3; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: #854d0e;">
      Beta software — expect false positives and false negatives.</p>

